      "subject": "feat(security): the Builder proves identity with its session token; Runtime stops trusting headers (SEC-1d, ADR-0043)",
      "body": "With real sign-in the Builder now sends the person's Supabase session token and no role, user or team header (ADR-0043 Decision 1); the development-only mock sign-in keeps the legacy headers. Once Runtime has an identity provider configured (SUPABASE_URL), caller headers are never believed from the browser, not even on this machine: a caller is a verified token, the internal token, a development identity configured in Runtime's environment, or anonymous. GET /api/runtime/identity reports how Runtime sees the caller (role, user id, source, reason; never a token), and the Executive Office Security heartbeat reads it live instead of preview text. Verified live with Supabase configured: a super_admin header from this machine is anonymous, a valid token is the verified super_admin, a forged token is rejected with bad_signature, and the browser preflight allows the Authorization header; runtime suites 435/435.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
